{"finish": true, "accepted": {"answer_type": "text", "value": "", "unit": "", "scale": "", "decision": "", "answer_text": "FY2023 (year ended June 30, 2023): Amcor completed three acquisitions, all within the Flexibles segment: (1) 100% of a Czech Republic company operating a flexible-packaging manufacturing plant (August 1, 2022; $59 million consideration); (2) 100% of a medical-device packaging manufacturing site in Shanghai, China (March 17, 2023; $60 million consideration, including up to $20 million contingent consideration); and (3) a New Zealand-based manufacturer of automated protein-packaging machines (May 31, 2023; $45 million consideration, including up to $13 million contingent consideration). The filing says their aggregate effect was not material to Amcor’s consolidated financial statements.

FY2022: No acquisitions are disclosed in the acquisitions-and-divestitures note. The reported activity was instead disposal of non-core Flexibles assets.

FY2021: No acquisitions are disclosed in that note. The reported activity was divestiture of a non-core European hospital-supplies business, two non-core businesses in India and Argentina, and sale of the AMVIG equity investment.", "citations": [{"receipt_id": "r7", "document_id": "AMCOR_2023_10K", "page": 64}, {"receipt_id": "r8", "document_id": "AMCOR_2023_10K", "page": 64}, {"receipt_id": "r9", "document_id": "AMCOR_2023_10K", "page": 65}]}, "observation": {"raw_chars": 1425, "truncated": false}}

